{"availability":"available","full":"malikrajat/rm-colorful-console-logger","name":"rm-colorful-console-logger","description":"A lightweight library for colorful console logging with filename and line number.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":16,"forks":0,"created":"2024-12-01T08:43:31Z","updated":"2026-07-26T08:05:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitejs-vite-uufslecf","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:45:16.058Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:45:16.058Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:45:16.058Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:47.331Z","stars":16,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T23:45:16.058Z","stars":16,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Universal colorful console logging for every JavaScript environment — Node.js, Deno, Bun, browsers, React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, Next.js, Electron, and more.","rm-colorful-console-logger is a lightweight, developer-friendly logging library that allows you to print colorful, structured messages to the browser console. It automatically captures the filename and line number of the caller, making debugging faster and more intuitive.","The library is extremely lightweight with a minimal footprint. Check the badges at the top of this README for the latest minzipped size."],"features":["Log messages in vibrant colors.","Automatically fetches the file and line number of the caller.","Compatible with every major JavaScript environment and framework: Angular, React, Vue.js, Svelte, Next.js, Nuxt.js, Node.js, Deno, Bun, Electron, React Native, Expo, and vanilla JavaScript/TypeScript.","Works in browser, server (SSR/SSG), CLI tools, desktop apps, mobile apps, edge runtimes, and test environments.","Zero dependencies. Framework-agnostic. Tree-shakable. ESM-first."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/malikrajat/rm-colorful-console-logger/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"11be65dc